    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** serving as our undisputed anchor, posting a robust 64.45 efficiency score against Ray Kerr. Despite the left-on-left dynamic, **Kyle Tucker** remains an auto-start; his pedigree and expected volume in the cleanup spot far outweigh the marginal 1% platoon dip. **Andy Pages** also makes the cut with a 52.74 score, leveraging a neutral platoon advantage to secure a UTIL spot. While **Drake Baldwin** faces the stiffest test of our starters against the 3.22 xERA of Blake Snell, his projected role at the heart of the order provides enough counting stat upside to justify the 44.76 score, though he remains a high-risk play. **Jackson Merrill** rounds out the outfield with a 49.97 rating; he is the most intriguing play of the day given his speed profile, which provides vital assistance in our pursuit of stolen bases, even against a tough arm in Henderson.\n\nOur toughest bench decision involved **Dominic Smith**, who finished at 32.47\u2014well below our start threshold. While the optimizer looked closely at his BvP and lineup potential, the combination of facing Snell\u2019s elite peripheral numbers and a suboptimal #8 spot in the order relegated him to the pine to preserve our remaining game caps. Elsewhere, the roster remains thinned by unfortunate scheduling and health: **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are completely unavailable due to team off-days, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL. We are continuing to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Liam Hicks**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, **Franklin Arias**, and **Henry Bolte**, but for today, the focus is squarely on whether the primary lineup can navigate the challenging opposing pitching effectively. We will remain hyper-vigilant for any final lineup adjustments that could shift the scoring for **Drake Baldwin**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages** before first pitch.",
